# Line endings are LF, everywhere, for everyone.
#
# This repository is worked on from WSL and from Windows against the same
# working tree, and Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf = true` in its system
# config. Without the rule below, a `git add` from the Windows side announces
# that it will rewrite every LF file to CRLF, and the two sides disagree about
# what the file on disk should look like.
#
# `.gitattributes` beats `core.autocrlf`, so this settles it in the repository
# rather than in one machine's configuration: text files are stored with LF and
# checked out with LF on every platform. `text=auto` still lets Git detect
# binary content and leave it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files this repository actually holds. Anything Git
# might misread as text stays byte-exact.
*.rs      text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.lock    text eol=lf
justfile  text eol=lf

*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.pdf     binary
